#: ../../../contributing.rst:155
msgid "Lint Tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:157
msgid ""
"Linting runs through `pre-commit <https://pre-commit.com/>`_, wired into the "
"``lint`` tox environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:159
msgid "$ tox run -e lint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:163
msgid ""
"The main hooks are ``ruff-check`` and ``ruff-format`` (lint and format "
"Python), ``codespell`` (spelling), ``mdformat`` (Markdown, wrapped at 120), "
"``yamlfmt`` (YAML), ``pyproject-fmt`` (``pyproject.toml``), and ``flake8-"
"lazy``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:166
msgid ""
"``flake8-lazy`` keeps the ``__lazy_modules__`` list at the top of each pipx "
"module up to date. On Python 3.15 and later (:pep:`810`) the modules it "
"lists load on first use rather than at import, which shortens CLI startup; "
"older Pythons ignore the list. The hook rewrites the list itself, so when it "
"fails, review and stage its change. A module whose import has a side effect "
"that must happen at startup (reading environment variables or terminal "
"state) belongs in ``standalone.lazy-exclude-modules`` under ``[tool.flake8-"
"lazy]`` in ``pyproject.toml``."
msgstr ""

