"drift from the commands. For a live-reloading preview while editing, use "
"``tox run -e docs-live``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:222
msgid "Releasing New ``pipx`` Versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:224
msgid ""
"The protected pre-release workflow determines the next version from the "
"fragment types, builds the changelog, runs ``release-creator contributors`` "
"to add a *New Contributors* subsection, formats the changelog with ``prek``, "
"and prepares a patch. The repository-scoped App then pushes the release "
"commit and annotated tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:229
msgid "Initiating a Release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:231
msgid ""
"Run **Pre-release** from the Actions tab on ``main``. Choose ``auto`` to "
"calculate the version from the fragments, or choose ``major``, ``minor``, or "
"``patch`` to override the bump. The input is a bump type, never a typed "
"version number. To preview the same inputs locally without pushing, run "
"``python scripts/release.py`` or ``python scripts/release.py --bump minor`` "
"from an installed ``release`` dependency group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:237
msgid "What Happens During Release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:239
msgid ""
"The tag starts the release workflow. It builds the sdist and wheel with "
"locked build dependencies, and builds ``pipx.pyz`` from the wheel and the "
"runtime dependencies locked for the zipapp targets. In parallel it renders "
"Markdown notes from that tag's RST changelog. Once the zipapp passes its "
"smoke test, the distributions go to `PyPI <https://pypi.org>`_ with `trusted "
"publishing <https://docs.pypi.org/trusted-publishers/>`_. After ``PyPI`` has "
"the expected files, a single step creates the GitHub Release with the zipapp "
"attached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:245
msgid ""
"Retry a failed run with \"Re-run failed jobs\", which uploads the same built "
"files; the release job checks their SHA256 digests against ``PyPI`` before "
"it writes the GitHub Release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:249
msgid "Version Calculation Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.rst:251
msgid ""
"Starting from ``1.8.0``, ``auto`` with a feature becomes ``1.9.0`` and "
"``auto`` with only bug fixes becomes ``1.8.1``. Selecting ``major`` yields "
"``2.0.0``, ``minor`` yields ``1.9.0``, and ``patch`` yields ``1.8.1``. "
"Removing support for an older Python is a feature here because earlier pipx "
"releases remain installable on that interpreter."
msgstr ""
